# --- Secrets: this repository is public from the first commit, so these must
# --- never be committed. GitHub push protection is the second line of defence.
.env
.env.local
*.key

# Replies as they arrive. Only the ones approved for the demonstration are
# committed, and they go through scripts/approve_replies.py (R-07).
data/captured_replies/

# Replies taken back out of the published set while their publication basis is
# settled. They are kept so the captured responses remain available for audit
# and possible controlled replay, and they are kept out of the repository
# because whether they may be published is the open question. Recovering them from the history
# instead would not be the same thing: history can be rewritten, and a copy
# nobody has verified is not a copy.
data/withdrawn_from_publication/

# Replies waiting between being approved and being published. Publishing is
# all-or-nothing: a reply is written here first and moved into the published
# folder only when its manifest entry is written, so anything left here is an
# approval that did not finish. It sits inside the published folder, which is
# committed, so it is ignored rather than relied on to be empty: a file that
# never became published must not reach the repository by being nearby (R-11).
data/recorded_replies/.waiting_to_be_published/

# The screening samples as they were drawn, with the abstracts in them. The
# labels beside them are prepared for public release; the abstracts are not,
# because publishing somebody else's abstract needs a basis nobody has
# established (R-12). What the rule governs is what may leave the working
# copy.
data/hand_screened_sample/drawn_for_screening/

# The CLEF review's records as fetched, and every measurement run's output,
# which holds the model's summaries and extracts of them. Same rule as the
# draw above: the identifiers and labels beside this folder are committed, the
# text of the papers is not (TF-03, R-12).
data/clef_tar/private/

# Buffers written at the hand-over between the two agents (ID-10). Every run
# writes one, and it holds the abstracts and open-access full text the run
# retrieved. Publishing retrieved text is a deliberate act, not something a run
# should do on its own, which is the same rule the captured replies follow. A
# buffer kept as evidence is added on purpose with "git add -f".
evidence/sample_run/*.json

# The run log holds what one run did on one day, and is appended to as it
# works. Kept for the same reason the buffer is (FR-15, ID-10).
evidence/run_log.jsonl

# Local databases and caches (evidence is committed deliberately, not by accident)
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.cache/
http_cache/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
.Rhistory
